<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia June qtr house starts fall 3.2 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia June qtr house starts fall 3.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian dwelling unit building commencements fell 3.2 percent in the June quarter over the March quarter to 30,446 for a year-on-year fall of 16.4 percent, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>Analysts had, on average, expected housing starts to fall 3.0 percent in the June quarter.  </p>
<p>Australian housing starts, June qtr-</p>
<p>    Private Sector:			s/adj	  orig</p>
<p>    Houses				   20,068	 20,325</p>
<p>    Total private residential	  29,089	 29,350</p>
<p>Public Sector:</p>
<p>    Houses				   n/a	    370</p>
<p>    Total Public			   n/a	    1,491</p>
<p>    Private/Public Houses		20,356	 20,695</p>
<p>    Total residential		    30,446	 30,841</p>
<p>The bureau said the March quarter seasonally adjusted commencements were revised to a 6.0 percent rise from the originally reported 4.4 percent, taking total commencement to 31,451.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
